@startuml notifications_inbox
title Notifications: WebSocket, offline recovery and settings
autonumber
actor "User" as User
participant "CLI / TUI" as Client
participant "CLI internal/app" as ClientApp
participant "Live client\nSeparate streaming contract" as Live
participant "Document client\nHTTP OR gRPC adapter" as Document
box "hermes-document-service" #E0F4E0
participant "API + middleware" as API
participant "internal/app\nIncluding proposed settings" as App
participant "internal/postgres" as Repo
participant "internal/redis/settings\nPROPOSED" as Settings
end box
database "Document PostgreSQL" as DB
database "Redis\nSessions + proposed settings/PubSub" as Redis
participant "notification-service\nInstance A" as HNS
participant "notification-service\nInstance B" as OtherHNS
database "Notification PostgreSQL\nPending offline messages" as Pending

== Connect / reconnect ==
User -> Client : Open TUI / explicitly start live reception
Client -> ClientApp : Start live connection using selected session
ClientApp -> Live : Connect(token)
Live -> HNS : WebSocket handshake over TLS
HNS -> Redis : Validate session using shared contract (ADR-001)
alt Invalid session or Redis unavailable
  HNS --> Live : Unauthenticated / temporarily unavailable; no connection
  Live --> ClientApp : Error
  ClientApp --> Client : Sign-in required / retryable connection error
else Valid session
  Redis --> HNS : Authenticated user_id and session identity
  HNS -> HNS : Register local connection; coordinate online routing (OPEN)
  ref over HNS, Redis
    Load current user settings (ADR-003 proposed Redis representation).
    Settings absence/unavailability behavior and authorization source remain OPEN.
  end ref
  HNS --> Live : Connected
  Live --> ClientApp : Connection established
end
note over ClientApp, HNS
  Live streaming is a separate client contract from InboxRemote.
  Long-lived connection ownership and reconnect/backoff need client design;
  do not reinterpret existing HTTP/GRPC inbox adapters as WebSocket adapters.
  One-shot CLI operations do not imply a persistent WebSocket.
end note

== Recover pending offline messages ==
ref over HNS, Pending
  For a valid connection, coordinate pending-message recovery with live routing.
  One connecting session receives accumulated messages (arch/notes.txt).
  Exclusive claim/lease, batching and concurrent connection protocol remain OPEN.
end ref
HNS -> Pending : Read/claim user's pending messages under agreed protocol
Pending --> HNS : Batch / empty / unavailable
HNS -> HNS : Recheck applicable visibility and recipient ownership (source OPEN)
HNS -> Live : Send pending batch to selected connection
Live -> ClientApp : Recovered messages
ClientApp --> Client : Display after terminal is available
note over HNS, Pending
  Client ack, removal/marking, retry after disconnect and claim release are OPEN.
  Do not delete messages merely because a socket write succeeded.
  Fan-out of this backlog to other sessions and permanent history are not required.
  Incoming live messages go to all active connections (events_dispatch.puml).
end note

== Open a notification target ==
User -> Client : Open target from a message
Client -> ClientApp : Documents.Get / Workspaces.Get / Users.GetPublicProfile(target_id)
ClientApp -> Document : Query target through owning service adapter
Document -> API : Protected domain read
ref over API, App : Validate session through Auth + Redis (auth.puml)
API -> App : Query(authenticated actor, target_id)
App -> Repo : Read active target with CURRENT domain access predicate
Repo -> DB : Access-filtered SELECT
Repo --> App : Accessible object / unavailable
App --> API : Allowed DTO / error
API --> Document : Result
Document --> ClientApp : Model / error
ClientApp --> Client : Show target or unavailable
note over ClientApp, App
  HNS delivers a message/target reference, not document contents via GetTarget.
  A message does not grant access. Minimal deletion/removal notices
  contain no inaccessible document content and may have no openable target.
end note

== Optional durable inbox / read state ==
ref over ClientApp, Pending
  OPEN: ListInbox, pagination, unread count, MarkRead / MarkAllRead contracts.
  If retained: recipient ownership + current visibility govern items AND counts;
  mark-all uses a boundary that excludes later arrivals.
  Offline recovery does not itself imply permanent history or read receipts.
end ref

== Proposed settings update (ADR-003) ==
User -> Client : Enable/disable notification category
Client -> ClientApp : Settings.Update(category, enabled, expected_version)
ClientApp -> Document : Update user settings
Document -> API : Protected request
ref over API, App : Validate session through Auth + Redis
API -> App : Proposed Settings.Update(authenticated actor, request)
App -> Repo : Transaction: read current settings, check version, persist changes
Repo -> DB : BEGIN; UPDATE settings/version; COMMIT / ROLLBACK
Repo --> App : Confirmed durable settings / error
alt PostgreSQL update confirmed
  App -> Settings : Synchronize versioned user settings via owned interface
  Settings -> Redis : Update representation only if version is newer;\nexplicit PUBLISH UserSettingsChanged(user_id, version)
  Redis --> Settings : Synchronized / failed / unknown
  Settings --> App : Synchronization outcome
  note over App, Redis
    Proposal, not a cross-store transaction.
    Durable-write success followed by Redis failure needs retry/reconciliation.
    API status for "saved but not propagated", atomic Redis write/PUBLISH
    and maximum propagation delay remain OPEN.
  end note
else PostgreSQL update rejected / failed
  App -> App : Do not publish an uncommitted settings change
end
App --> API : Settings result under agreed partial-failure contract (OPEN)
API --> Document : Result
Document --> ClientApp : Result

== Proposed propagation to every HNS instance ==
Redis -> HNS : Pub/Sub UserSettingsChanged(user_id, version)
Redis -> OtherHNS : Same signal on every subscribed HNS instance
HNS -> Redis : Reload current versioned settings
OtherHNS -> Redis : Reload current versioned settings
Redis --> HNS : Current settings/version
Redis --> OtherHNS : Current settings/version
HNS -> HNS : Apply to ALL local connections of this user
OtherHNS -> OtherHNS : Apply to ALL local connections of this user
note over Redis, OtherHNS
  New connections load current settings; subscription/load race must be closed.
  Pub/Sub has no replay: on reconnect resync connected users;
  proposed periodic version checks repair missed signals.
  Reordered/stale signals must not roll settings back.
  Settings are not workspace authorization.
end note

== Disconnect, expiry or revocation ==
Live -> HNS : Connection closed / transport failure
HNS -> HNS : Unregister local connection; update routing under agreed protocol
note over Live, HNS
  Logout/expiry/account deletion while socket remains open needs policy (ADR-001).
  No claim of instantaneous remote socket revocation.
  Reconnect authenticates again; gap recovery/acknowledgements remain OPEN.
  During external editing, preserve local draft and restore UI independently
  from live transport; refreshing domain state does not guarantee message replay.
end note
@enduml
